task(GIT-HISTORY-REWRITE-2026-08-03):
  title    = "origin disposition after the S5-approved 2026-08-03 filter-repo purge (no shared ancestor)"
  status   = done
  priority = media
  date     = "2026-08-10"
  owner    = "rmw3 [H] decides origin disposition — [O] measured the state, cannot decide it"
  context:
    "On 2026-08-03 04:17 a `git filter-repo` run rewrote this repository. The run left its own
     run record in .git/filter-repo/ — this is recorded fact, not inference:
       changed-refs : main · feat/ds-s1 · a0-classifier-chain-fix  (all three)
       commit-map   : 1672 commits remapped
       first-changed: 75bf022 → d484c8d
       ref-map      : b1e2ffb → 9e9ba52  main
                      299717d → c6d5178  feat/ds-s1
                      7cc9672 → 13ebd3d  a0-classifier-chain-fix
     Three side effects of filter-repo, all observed live and all explained by it:
       - .git/refs/remotes/ empty while the fetch refspec is intact — filter-repo DELETES the origin
         remote by design (so rewritten history cannot be pushed to the old remote by reflex); origin
         was later re-added, which restored the default refspec but not the tracking refs.
       - main's reflog empty and HEAD's reflog starting exactly at 2026-08-03 04:41 — reflogs expired.
       - b1e2ffb (origin/main at the last fetch, .git/FETCH_HEAD 2026-08-03 04:14) and d5e701f (the
         sha task(BRANCH-RECONCILE) cited as pushed) resolve to nothing — objects gc-pruned.
     CONSEQUENCE, and the reason this is alta: ref-map shows origin/main's b1e2ffb IS local main's
     9e9ba52 — same content, different sha. Local and origin therefore carry the SAME WORK on
     histories with NO common ancestor from 75bf022/d484c8d onward. `git push` to origin is rejected
     as non-fast-forward; there is no merge path, because merge needs an ancestor and there is none.
     THIS WAS DELIBERATE, S5-DECIDED, AND RECORDED — see task(NATS-TOKEN-ROTATION-2026-08-03), whose
     `remaining` field specified this exact operation in advance ('a full history purge (git
     filter-repo + force-push + worktree resync for .claude/worktrees/fix-a0-classifier-chain) is a
     separate, higher-risk operation NOT done here — needs its own deliberate S5 decision'), and
     current_focus.json(CLIMA-NATS-OBSERVABILITY-INCIDENT-2026-08-02), which records it executed:
     'git history purge done (feat/ds-s1, filter-repo, verified token absent from every object,
     nothing was ever pushed to origin so no public exposure ever existed ... incl. the
     main-branch-hash side effect)'. Purpose: purge the leaked NATS token from history.
     ⟹ the origin consequence was ALREADY KNOWN ('the main-branch-hash side effect') and the
     exposure question ALREADY ANSWERED (nothing was ever pushed). The only genuinely open item is
     which disposition origin gets — see design."
  design:
    "Three mutually exclusive dispositions, all rmw3's call — [O] does not pick one:
     (1) force-push local → origin. Any existing clone of origin breaks and must re-clone.
     (2) re-create the GitHub repo from local and abandon the old one.
     (3) treat origin as dead; local git is canon; revisit at public release.
     Whichever is chosen, record it here in the same commit that executes it."
  gating   = "rmw3 decision — no technical blocker, and no option is reversible by merge"
  files    = []
  disposition_2026_08_15: "CLOSED by rmw3 decision (2026-08-15, S5): option (1) force-push.
      Only user clones; no conflicts; key already revoked at Google console
      (2026-08-15, rmw3 confirmed). Executed:
        git push origin main --force-with-lease   b1e2ffbd → aa47ca8f (forced)
        git push origin feat/ds-s1 --force-with-lease e8a091aa → 71f0c798 (forced)
      Verified post-push (R4): git ls-remote origin shows aa47ca8f (main) +
      71f0c798 (feat/ds-s1); git grep -l OLD-KEY origin/main and
      origin/feat/ds-s1 both EMPTY — old key no longer visible in the live
      history of either branch. GitHub may still hold orphaned objects until
      GC (90-day window) — closed risk because the key was revoked first.
      Decision recorded in the same commit that executed it (R4.1)."
  correction_2026_08_10: "This task was FILED WITH A FALSE CLAIM and is corrected here in the same
      session. It asserted the rewrite 'left NO record in HANDOFF.vsm.md, TASKS.vsm, or
      docs/incidents/'. That was wrong twice over: TASKS.vsm(NATS-TOKEN-ROTATION-2026-08-03) named
      the operation in advance and current_focus.json recorded it done, with the origin side effect
      already noted. Cause of the error: the grep that 'found no record' DID match TASKS.vsm's
      'git filter-repo' line — the match was cut off by a `head -8` whose slots were consumed by
      unrelated BFG hits, and the focus note carrying the answer was truncated at 110 chars by the
      reader's own print. Same defect [O] recorded about itself in HANDOFF session
      2026-08-10-claude-attenuator-close ('diagnosing a line from output my own cut had truncated'),
      repeated inside the session that quoted it. The residue is narrow: origin disposition only.
      Open, unchanged by this correction: theme D's 'BFG history review' gate is still written as
      pending in HANDOFF.vsm.md while a filter-repo run has since happened — that needs
      re-examination, which this task does NOT do."

