      El child SÍ tiene su S5 local básico (pre-commit + checks
      child-boot-valid/plugins-port-verify + verify_child.py) desde
      RECTIF-CHILD-S5-LOCAL (done) — falta esta política específica.
      RESUELTO 2026-08-15: despachada (RECTIF-CHILD-DESTRUCTIVE, envelope +
      task child CHILD-DESTRUCTIVE-GATE; child commit e956314). La
      verificación del commit del child (R4) queda en esa task open.",
}

fact("child-sessions-survive-process-kill") = {
  body:  "OpenCode persists all sessions (parent AND child) in
      ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db (SQLite). Killing a tmux
      session or the opencode process does NOT lose the conversation —
      it can be resumed with the session id (found e.g. via
      'SELECT id,title,directory FROM session ORDER BY time_updated DESC').",
  why:   "2026-08-11: the child's hung session was killed; the whole
      conversation remained recoverable. Knowing this changes the damage
      assessment of any accidental kill — but does NOT make the kill
      acceptable without confirmation.",
  apply: "Before mourning a killed agent session, check opencode.db first.
      Before killing one, still ask rmw3 first (task DESTRUCTIVE-ACTION-EXPLICIT-OK).",
}

